{title: As The River Runs}
{artist: Larry Holder / Elton Smith}
{time: 4/4}
{key: Am}
{tempo: 99}

Lyrics
[Am]As [F]a [Dm]river [G]runs to meet the [G]sea,
[Em]I [F]run [F]to [Am]You.
[Am7]Lord, [Em7]your grace [Em]is all I [Am7]ever [C]need;
Your [F]love [F]is [A]true.
Your [G7]abundant [G]mercy flows [A#]to [G#]me;
[Fmaj7]I [E]know You care,
For as [D]the river [G]runs [Em7]to meet [G]the sea,
[Am7]I run [F]and find You there.
[Em]Glory to Your Name;
With [Gm7]joy [Gm]my soul [G7]proclaims
[G]That You [E7]are all-sufficient, [Am7]Lord;
Your mercy's still the [C]same.
[Dm7]Glory [G]all to You;
[Gm7]Praise for [G7]all [G]You do.
[Cmaj7]By [E7]grace alone, I [E]live [Am]each [G]day:
[Am]My [Fmaj7]soul is born [Em]anew!
[C]As a forest [Em]longs [G]for [Am7]gentle [Em]rain,
[C]I [Fmaj7]long [Fmaj7]for [Am]You.
[G]For Your gentle shower [Em7]of love [Am7]and [E]grace
[Gm]Makes [Fmaj7]all things [A]new.
Your [Em]abundant [G]mercy [C]flows [A#]to [Fmaj7]me;
I [F7]know [Fm7]You care,
For as the [Em7]forest waits the [Am7]coming rain,
I wait and find You [C]there.
Glory [Am7]to [G]Your [C]Name;
[C]With joy [Gm7]my soul [G]proclaims
[D]That [Cm]You [E7]are all-sufficient, [Am7]Lord;
[C]Your [Fmaj7]mercy falls like rain.
Glory all [G7]to You;
[Em]Praise [Gm7]for [G7]all You [C]do.
[Cmaj7]By grace [E]alone, I [Am7]live [Em]each day:
[A]My soul [D]is [G7]born anew!
[C]And [Em]forever, [Fmaj7]Lord, I [Em7]see
[Am7]That in You [Dm7]my soul is [Gm7]free:
[Gm]And [E7]to [F]You [Fmaj7]Lord, may [Em7]I run to [A]find
[Am7]My [Dm7]every [Am]need,
As [A#maj7]a river runs [Am7]to meet the sea!
